  "source": "overnight-assemble-overlay",
  "summary": "Rates markets entered a heavy policy day with front-end tightening already baked in and long-end yields still elevated but off recent highs. Official SOFR sits at 3.93% with March 2027 futures about 55bp above cash and a September peak near 4.69%; surveys lean to a Fed hold on 28 October, yet hawkish guidance would challenge recent bullish Treasury positioning. Canada's CORRA path is steeper still: March sits about 76bp over 2.24% cash, and one-month contracts already imply a near-term hike ahead of the same-day Bank of Canada decision. Oil remains a wedge \u2014 WTI near $100 and Brent near $114 on Hormuz disruption and thin spare capacity \u2014 while equities hold firm, with the S&P around 7723 and the VIX near 18. Euro and the Canadian dollar are still weak versus the dollar. New Zealand inflation could not be verified, so NZ-specific new risk stays off the board. Next: the Federal Reserve and Bank of Canada statements, whether energy risk stays bid, and whether AI-credit headlines spill into duration.",
  "type": "OVERNIGHT_ACCEPTED_PUBLIC_NEWS"
}
